<section class="sec sec-white"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head rv"><span class="kicker">Regions</span><h2>How claims change across New Mexico</h2><p>The same policy language plays out very differently in a Santa Fe adobe, a Rio Rancho tract home and a Ruidoso cabin.</p></div><div class="index-list" data-stagger><div class="plain-card rv"><h2>Middle Rio Grande</h2><p>The state’s largest housing market. Stucco ranch homes in the Northeast Heights, flat-roofed Pueblo Revival houses near the river and pitched-roof subdivisions on the West Mesa all take hail differently.</p><p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0">Albuquerque · Rio Rancho · Los Lunas</p></div><div class="plain-card rv"><h2>Northern Mountains &amp; Four Corners</h2><p>Elevation changes everything: adobe and historic-district rules in Santa Fe, wildfire exposure in the Jemez and Sangre de Cristo foothills, and hard freezes that split pipes.</p><p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0">Santa Fe · Los Alamos · Farmington · Taos</p></div><div class="plain-card rv"><h2>Eastern Plains &amp; Pecos Valley</h2><p>Open country where spring and summer storms can drop very large hail and spin up tornadoes. Oilfield growth adds commercial yards, apartments and new subdivisions to the claim mix.</p><p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0">Clovis · Roswell · Hobbs · Carlsbad</p></div><div class="plain-card rv"><h2>Southern Desert &amp; Sacramento Mountains</h2><p>Desert wind and monsoon downbursts around Las Cruces and the Tularosa Basin, and fire-then-flood risk in the forested mountains above Ruidoso.</p><p style="font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0">Las Cruces · Alamogordo · Ruidoso</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="cta-band"><div class="wrap"><div class="in rv"><div><h2>Don’t see your town?</h2><p>We cover every New Mexico county. Call and tell us where the property is.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line" href="/contact-new-mexico-appraiser/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></div></section>
